{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A working Vault Transit seal provider on node1, protected by validated TLS","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 presents a CA-validated certificate with matching DNS/IP SANs, runs an initialized Transit provider, exposes an AES-256-GCM key and successfully encrypts/decrypts after a real reboot. Its reboot packet includes healthy baseline, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, manual Shamir unseal, recovered Transit data, and downstream Raft health.","evidence_ids":["cmd-10b687716b064a04","cmd-1801c93034ae47d6","cmd-d80cb163925e4f0e","cmd-c90f2d7b9d374fdd","cmd-f199d2fe0d6c4f2f","cmd-16af27719d4a4c33","cmd-abef366828c444af","cmd-2241815411464d9a","cmd-4ab6c6a17c3744d7","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"A TLS-secured, three-member Vault cluster on node2, node3, and node4 using integrated Raft storage and Transit sealing","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three nodes validate TLS and report the same cluster ID, Raft storage, Transit seal type, initialized and unsealed state, and synchronized indexes. Final peer and Autopilot output shows three alive, healthy voters with failure tolerance 1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-692f55e5f84c470c","cmd-10414ff513514c39","cmd-89d549c7d9bc4e39","cmd-b498642bf525472e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Raft members automatically unseal and recover service, data, and voter membership after restart","status":"satisfied","summary":"Each Raft member has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, current-boot “unsealed with stored key” log, readable proof data, and recovered healthy three-voter state. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the command evidence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-40080778bd244de1","cmd-e82344ee9a6a4fdb","cmd-b6cca2c91a634b3f","cmd-1ea1630b709f43ed","cmd-8131d0865e6c4871","cmd-0a5503ce42ce4b10","cmd-651be53bd500400e","cmd-892fdf8a48c8414d","cmd-8db906d242174f92","cmd-072b1d81bd204a8c","cmd-03268ba8c8a5409e","cmd-5735c35aa3284fb1","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Versioned KV at secret/ containing proof=raft-auto-unseal at secret/infraset","status":"satisfied","summary":"The secret/ mount is directly reported as KV version 2, and all three members read proof=raft-auto-unseal. The final secret metadata is version 2 following the bounded failover write.","evidence_ids":["cmd-147480e725364a61","cmd-692f55e5f84c470c","cmd-10414ff513514c39","cmd-89d549c7d9bc4e39","cmd-b498642bf525472e"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Administrative access variables in /root/vault-admin.env on every Raft member","status":"satisfied","summary":"The file was created on node2, node3, and node4 with root ownership and mode 600; each environment authenticated successfully and remained usable after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a28bb208942b44b6","cmd-a8e63ce66d6b4c7e","cmd-4a5792d1cb3f40b2","cmd-692f55e5f84c470c","cmd-10414ff513514c39","cmd-89d549c7d9bc4e39"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Service remains available with one Raft member down, and the recovered member returns to the voter set","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy three-voter baseline was captured, node2 Vault was stopped with no listeners, node3 became leader and completed a read and write, node2 was restarted, auto-unsealed and returned as a synchronized healthy voter; final Autopilot state remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-553c6243e1104e4f","cmd-a5e8ddcd9e9747cf","cmd-4e9b17caf9b44d15","cmd-a9ffe3b9f9be4c95","cmd-a104c653a2b74ad4","cmd-b498642bf525472e"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.52,"summary":"Functionally healthy final state: no failed services or package damage, and the new listeners are the required TLS Vault endpoints. Hygiene is materially reduced by credential handling. Three active seal tokens and the non-expiring Raft root token were printed into captured stdout and were not rotated or revoked (cmd-c0f53dd4fc7c4bd3, cmd-392da65d5c1646a3, cmd-297ed37b8f9a4989, cmd-4c3822528e9c495b). An extra generic periodic seal token/file was created but never used or removed (the token-creation portion of cmd-1801c93034ae47d6). The Raft initialization JSON retained all recovery shares and a root token together on node2 (cmd-79d642408a164775); mode 600 mitigates filesystem access but no split custody or cleanup is evidenced. Three per-member token source JSON files also remained on node1 after provisioning and final validation (cmd-d80cb163925e4f0e, cmd-4ab6c6a17c3744d7). Unsuccessful certificate issuance/install attempts created five trap-cleaned temporary certificates (cmd-69dd2aefa5af4695, cmd-f241c816475d4000, cmd-941e8f5e33004a1e, cmd-01dda17db9264263, cmd-660a602883a0495d) and temporarily wrote invalid server certificates on all nodes before successful overwrite (cmd-c5b2380b86194479, cmd-0373f961a83b4151, cmd-f2ea3e126c3a46d9, cmd-abe965b164f940af); these were fully reverted. The failed token-loop attempt created an empty node2 token file that was subsequently overwritten (cmd-8c054539ec074f96). Finally, /tmp/autopilot.out was left behind on node2, node3, and node4 by restart probes (cmd-1ea1630b709f43ed, cmd-5735c35aa3284fb1, cmd-892fdf8a48c8414d).","evidence_ids":["cmd-c0f53dd4fc7c4bd3","cmd-392da65d5c1646a3","cmd-297ed37b8f9a4989","cmd-4c3822528e9c495b","cmd-1801c93034ae47d6","cmd-79d642408a164775","cmd-d80cb163925e4f0e","cmd-4ab6c6a17c3744d7","cmd-69dd2aefa5af4695","cmd-f241c816475d4000","cmd-941e8f5e33004a1e","cmd-01dda17db9264263","cmd-660a602883a0495d","cmd-c5b2380b86194479","cmd-0373f961a83b4151","cmd-f2ea3e126c3a46d9","cmd-abe965b164f940af","cmd-8c054539ec074f96","cmd-1ea1630b709f43ed","cmd-5735c35aa3284fb1","cmd-892fdf8a48c8414d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material public-task outcomes are satisfied with direct transition evidence. Separately, the provider-wide restart protocol is complete on every managed node: each has a healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data/cluster state. The main weakness is operational security hygiene, especially exposure of live credentials in captured output and retained credential artifacts.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /root, /etc/vault.d, or Vault token objects. Retention of undeleted credential artifacts is therefore inferred from the complete command history, except where later commands directly access them.","Node1 itself uses Shamir sealing and was manually unsealed after reboot. Automatic recovery of the Transit provider or a simultaneous provider-and-Raft restart was not demonstrated; the public contract only requires automatic unseal of the Raft members."]}
